// DF-172h: an `extern "C"` declared `-> Never` is the C `noreturn`
// declaration, and design 58 says a `-> Never` signature lowers to `void` +
// `noreturn`. The DEFINITION path did that; the DECLARATION path took
// `_get_llvm_type`'s i8 placeholder instead.
//
// That reached past the declaration, because an `@export`ed definition UNIFIES
// with a pre-existing bodyless declaration of the same symbol and inherits its
// type. So this exact arrangement — a module declaring the seam, another file
// defining it — emitted `define noundef i8 @d172h_stop(i32)` while the ABI
// document and every other spelling of `-> Never` said `void`. Harmless on the
// targets in tree, since nothing reads a diverging function's return register,
// and wrong everywhere it is written down.
//
// Found landing the SOS runtime seams (design 172 part 2), where `sos_rt_abort`
// is declared `-> Never` by `sosrt` and defined per side. What this test pins
// is the SHAPE — it compiles, links and diverges through the seam; the `void`
// half was verified from `--emit-ir` by hand, as DF-172b's check-freedom was.
// EXPECT: panic
// EXPECT-PANIC-CONTAINS: stopped at 7

import modules.never172h_stop

@export("d172h_stop")
func stop(code: UInt32) -> Never {
    panic("stopped at {}", code)
}

func main() {
    never172h_stop.halt(7u32)
}
